========================================================================
: NOTEBOOK SOURCES :
========================================================================
This place is served as official (and last) list of notes and notebooks
on lore. It is tool for organising sources via codes, so it is clear
which source adds to which part of lore, and how accurate it is.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
NAMING:
                        [t][q].[ac].[nm]_[dg]

[t] | type of source
    |-----------------|-----------------|
    |[N] - notebook   |[P] - paper      |

[q] | quality of source
    |----------------------|-----------------------|
    |[^] - well preserved  |[v] - badly preserved  |[None] - in between

[ac]| accuracy of source
    |-----------------|-----------|----------------|
    |[1] - accurate   |[2] - low  |[?] - disputed  |[x] - not friendly

[nm]| number of the source (three digits)

[dg]| 3-letter name of lore aspect shown in the source
    |-------------------|-----------------|
    |[lnd] - land, game |[map] - map      |
